      GET /signals/{vehicleID}/available
      GET /signals/{vehicleID}/live
      GET /signals/{vehicleID}/snapshot
      GET /signals/{vehicleID}/diff
      GET /signals/{vehicleID}/stats
      GET /signals/{vehicleID}/{signalName}/history
    All hook URLs in useTelemetry.ts already conform (no `/api/v1/`
    prefix; per-vehicle path-segment + snake_case query params).
  - internal/api/router.go L1718-1722 (Phase-42 / Prompt 0077): the
    `/signals/catalog` and `/signals/observations` routes were DELETED
    alongside `signal_catalog_handler.go`. The typed signal_log pipeline
    (migrations 000167+) + signal_handler.go's `/available` endpoint
    are now the authoritative catalog/observations surface.
  - internal/api/router.go L1594-1597 (/telemetry): GET /telemetry is
    served by telemetryHandler.TelemetryStatus — used by useMQTTStatus.
    Returns aggregate broker stats + per-vehicle streaming state. Hook
    correctly normalizes Record<vin,...> → array.
  - internal/api/router.go L897-902 (/tesla/fleet-telemetry): error VIN
    + error event endpoints unchanged. Hooks (useFleetTelemetryError*)
    correctly call them with no `/api/v1/` prefix.
  - internal/api/router.go L1286-1325 (/fsm): /fsm/stats and
    /fsm/transitions endpoints unchanged. useFSM.ts hooks correctly
    call them with snake_case query params (vehicle_id, fsm_type,
    hours, page, per_page).

Type cross-checks:
  - web/src/types/fsm/ui-types.ts: FSMStats, FSMTransitionResponse,
    FSMTransition all already use snake_case (vehicle_id, fsm_type,
    from_state, to_state, created_at, per_page) matching backend
    response shape. No change needed in useFSM.ts.
  - web/src/api/types.ts L1985: SignalHistoryResp is the canonical
    snake_case shape for the per-signal history endpoint. The pages
    that consume signal-history data (SignalLogViewerPage,
    SignalExplorerPage) already cast at the call site via
    `request<SignalHistoryResp>`, so the in-page typing is correct.
  - web/src/types/telemetry.ts: SignalHistoryResponse + SignalStats
    are camelCase legacy aliases. They are still used as the return
    type of useSignalHistory/useSignalLog/useSignalDiff/useSignalStats
    in useTelemetry.ts. Replacing them with SignalHistoryResp from
    api/types.ts would cascade-break out-of-scope consumers
    (LiveSignalSparklinesWidget.tsx accesses `p.valueNum` against the
    legacy camelCase shape). Per the locked-policy precedent
    established by Phase-43/0023 — only touch what is in scope, and
    do not rewrite hooks whose external consumers cannot be updated
    in this prompt's allowed-files window — we leave these legacy
    typings untouched. The widget is broken at runtime today (the
    backend returns snake_case `value_num`), but that is a
    pre-existing defect outside this prompt's scope.

SI conversion analysis (Phase-43 mandate):
  - All 6 telemetry pages are GENERIC raw-signal browsers. The values
    they render are arbitrary signals from the wire — `BatteryLevel`,
    `VehicleSpeed`, `OutsideTemp`, `Odometer`, `TPMSPressureFL`,
    `Gear`, `LightsHazardsOn`, etc. — and the unit semantics live in
    the signal NAME, not in the value. Applying convertDistanceFromSI
    to a raw `BatteryLevel` percent or a raw `Gear` enum would
    distort or destroy the displayed data.
  - SignalExplorerPage / SignalLogViewerPage / SignalDiffPage charts
    plot the raw signal numeric value on the Y axis with the signal
    name in the legend. There is no semantic "this is distance" or
    "this is speed" hint at the page level.
  - MQTTInspectorPage shows signal *counts*, *batches*, and
    *signals/sec throughput* — these are inherent integer counters
    and the Recharts AreaChart already plots the raw delta. No SI
    conversion is meaningful.
  - LiveSignalMonitorPage and SignalGapDetectorPage stringify raw
    values for display. No SI conversion appropriate.
  - Conclusion: NO useUnits / convertXFromSI integration is
    appropriate for the telemetry domain. This is the correct
    no-op outcome — telemetry is the unit-naive viewing surface
    and the rest of the app applies semantics on top.

Field-access audit (snake_case migration check):
  - SignalExplorerPage.tsx: maps SignalHistoryResp.data → SignalLogEntry
    using snake_case keys (created_at, value_num, value_str, value_bool).
    All chart/table renderers already read snake_case fields from rows.
  - SignalLogViewerPage.tsx: same mapping pattern; columns render
    snake_case fields directly.
  - SignalGapDetectorPage.tsx: reads /live response (Record<name,
    {value, timestamp}>), entry.value + entry.timestamp. Already
    matches backend shape.
  - SignalDiffPage.tsx: reads SignalDiffServerResponse.data →
    SignalDiffRow (snake_case name, value_a, value_b, source_a,
    source_b, age_ms_a, age_ms_b, changed). All renderers in
    SignalDiffTable.tsx read snake_case fields directly.
  - MQTTInspectorPage.tsx: reads VehicleTelemetry. Currently uses the
    camelCase aliases (signalCount, batchCount, signalsPerSecond,
    lastReceived) which the useMQTTStatus hook synthesises from the
    Record<vin, {snake_case}> backend response. That synthesis lives
    in the hook (L218-228) and is correct as-is.
  - LiveSignalMonitorPage.tsx: reads SSE event payload directly. No
    backend-typed fields — all access via dynamic Object.entries.

UNPORTABLE check: NONE. Every page renders fields the backend exposes.
