=== NOTES ===
Two notable mechanical decisions for this prompt:

(1) NO-OP-EXCEPT-DEPRECATION OUTCOME. Phase-43/0024 ports the
    features/telemetry domain. Unlike the vehicles/charging/driving/
    battery domains (where backend SI canonicalisation REQUIRED
    page-level conversion via useUnits / convertXFromSI), every page
    in features/telemetry/ is a GENERIC raw-signal viewer:

      - SignalExplorerPage / SignalLogViewerPage / SignalDiffPage:
        plot raw signal numeric values on chart Y-axes; the unit
        semantics live in the user-selected signal NAME, not in the
        page-level rendering code.
      - SignalGapDetectorPage / LiveSignalMonitorPage: stringify
        arbitrary raw signal values for display.
      - MQTTInspectorPage: shows broker counters + signals/sec
        throughput — inherent integer counts, no SI mapping.

    Applying convertDistanceFromSI to a raw BatteryLevel percent or
    a raw Gear enum would distort or destroy the data. The correct
    outcome for the telemetry domain is a NO-OP for SI conversion;
    the rest of the app applies semantics on top of these viewers.

    The only meaningful change is JSDoc @deprecated tags on
    useSignalCatalog and useSignalObservations — both call backend
    routes (/signals/catalog, /signals/observations) that
    Phase-42/0077 deleted alongside signal_catalog_handler.go. They
    are kept (not removed) because external out-of-scope features
    still import them: PowersharePage, AutopilotSection, GForcePanel,
    PedalUsage, SignalLogWidget, SignalCatalogWidget. This follows
    the locked-policy precedent established by Phase-43/0023 for
    useVampireDrainStats / useVampireDrainEvents.

(2) LEGACY HOOK RETURN TYPES PRESERVED. useSignalHistory /
    useSignalLog / useSignalDiff in useTelemetry.ts are typed against
    SignalHistoryResponse from web/src/types/telemetry.ts, which
    declares camelCase fields (valueNum, valueStr, valueBool). The
    REAL backend response is snake_case (value_num, value_str,
    value_bool) per web/src/api/types.ts:1985 SignalHistoryResp.

    Pages in scope (SignalLogViewerPage, SignalExplorerPage) already
    bypass the legacy typing by casting at the call site via
    request<SignalHistoryResp>, so the in-page typing is correct.

    Replacing the legacy hook return types with the canonical
    SignalHistoryResp would cascade-break out-of-scope consumers —
    specifically web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/
    LiveSignalSparklinesWidget.tsx accesses p.valueNum against the
    legacy camelCase shape. That widget is broken at runtime today
    (the backend returns snake_case), but that defect was pre-existing
    and lives outside this prompt's allowed-files window. Fixing it
    requires a separate prompt scoped to dashboard widgets.

(3) GATE WORKAROUNDS for Windows / PowerShell 7 quirks (consistent
    with Phase-43/0021 + Phase-43/0023 + Phase-46/64+65+69):
    - Resolve-Path the log file to absolute BEFORE Push-Location web,
      else Tee-Object loses the file under web\.github\... once cwd
      changes inside the BUILD step.
    - Use .\node_modules\.bin\tsc.cmd and 
pm.cmd run build
      (rather than 
px tsc / 
pm run build) because pwsh -File
      invocation triggers npm 10's "could not determine executable to
      run" error.
    - Use the audit grep regex with simple ['"] character class
      (PS double-quoted string + escaped quotes) rather than the
      verbatim prompt-script's [\\\\\""] form, which fails to
      parse cleanly on PowerShell 7 when copied through the tool
      boundary.

